Store reviewable model, feature, training, evaluation, and runtime configurations here. Prefer immutable or digestible configuration identity for consequential runs. Do not store credentials or host secrets.

Link configurations to the experiment dimension map and current slice in [the research architecture](../RESEARCH_ARCHITECTURE.md#experiment-dimensions-and-current-slice), or to the established protocol/design owner it names. Expand configuration and arm IDs into their effective settings, including valid combinations and nested or bundled choices. Keep training loss, learning-rate policy, checkpoint selection, and evaluation metric/horizon separately identifiable even when one arm chooses several together.

Count logical training identities from valid combinations and repeats. Keep execution attempts and score views separate; rescoring one prediction artifact at several horizons does not by itself create more training runs. Preserve the accepted configuration identity and record any observed run deviation against its source.
